& [AuthorityLineage] is coordinated and prospective
  + phase3 machine forms signature ae44deed-29c7-4a6a-96d1-1a0091539575 remains immutable history and is superseded for current selected machine-form meaning
  + topology forms signature 0e2cfacb-8659-41c2-b804-0eb1b49ff5b2 remains immutable history and is superseded for current selected topology-form meaning
  + replacement machine-forms signature c681b74d-7543-43be-96a1-a8ccb89181fb governs only its exact module scope
  + replacement topology-forms signature 1edee945-9957-41d7-bd17-0765ec54f5cb governs only its exact module scope
  + both replacement signatures bind this same canonical path, phase lock, source, and joint implementation milestone
  + implementation may begin only while both signatures are valid
  + historical proof artifacts retain original bytes and then-current meaning rather than being rewritten

& [TermRoles] are closed
  + [evidence] is inspectable support whose lineage and admissibility a consumer must verify
  + [evidence_label] names a support grade but does not create its support
  + [form_validity] is pure syntax and relation validation over supplied values
  + [actual_acquisition] is a separately authorized physical producer event with retained lineage
  + [issuer_proof] is a separately authorized binding between support, receipt content, and issuer authority
  + [consumer_decision] is a separately authorized freshness, single-use, policy, and operational judgment
  + [world_state] is an external condition that no current enum value directly proves
  - never: treat enum construction, serde success, form validation, digest equality, or public receipt construction as acquisition, issuance, or world-state proof

& [NonAtomicRepeatedInventoryEqualMeaning] is exact
  + NonAtomic denies snapshot, transaction, tree lock, uninterrupted interval, and platform immutability
  + RepeatedInventory requires two actual complete physical inventory acquisitions
  + first acquisition completes before second acquisition begins or an equally precise separately evidenced order exists
  + both acquisitions use exact common scanner, encoding, limits, root, policy, and comparison scope
  + each acquisition retains independent complete lineage and canonical ordered-inventory digest
  + both carriers pass current independent pure rederivation
  + exact pure reconciliation disposition is Equal
  + equality concerns only canonical committed inventory subjects in that exact common scope
  + intermediate change-and-restore remains possible
  + change after the second acquisition remains possible
  + unobserved external writers remain possible
  + freshness beyond separately bound issue and expiry rules is not implied
  - never: infer quiescence, atomicity, immutability, stability, admission, mutation safety, seal validity, or promotion eligibility

& [OsSnapshotProvenMeaning] is reserved and currently inadmissible
  + the label means a separately authorized producer bound inventory to an identified platform snapshot primitive with exact provenance
  + pure enum validity never proves the primitive, snapshot, producer, view, lifetime, or acquisition exists
  + this revision retains the value to preserve the already delineated evidence lattice
  + TopologyReceipt 0.3 rejects the value because no snapshot provenance fields exist
  + no conversion, downgrade, or fallback maps OsSnapshotProven to NonAtomicRepeatedInventoryEqual
  + future admission requires new source, schema, profile, producer, issuer, proof, and replacement authority

& [Phase3MachineFormsProfile] is revised exactly
  + PHASE3_MACHINE_FORMS_PROFILE is cantor-phase3-machine-forms/0.2
  + previous cantor-phase3-machine-forms/0.1 is not current implementation authority
  + no other Phase3 profile constant changes in this slice

& [InventoryConsistencyEvidenceContract] is exact
  + public type name is InventoryConsistencyEvidence
  + derive Clone, Copy, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, and Deserialize
  + serde rename_all is snake_case
  + exact variants are NonAtomicRepeatedInventoryEqual and OsSnapshotProven only
  + exact serialized values are non_atomic_repeated_inventory_equal and os_snapshot_proven
  + ValidatePhase3 remains pure and structurally accepts either closed variant
  + rustdoc beside the type states that structural validity is not acquisition, lineage, issuer, or world-state proof
  + no Default, Unknown, Other, catch-all, alias, type synonym, From, Into, public string parser, or compatibility wrapper exists

& [RemovedMachineFormsVocabulary] is strict
  + public ConsistencyClass is absent
  + public QuiescentDoubleInventory is absent
  + serialized quiescent_double_inventory is rejected
  + no deprecated re-export or conversion keeps old Rust callers compiling
  + current callers must make an explicit semantic revision

& [TopologyFormsProfiles] are revised exactly
  + TOPOLOGY_FORMS_PROFILE is cantor-phase3-topology-forms/0.3
  + TOPOLOGY_RECEIPT_PROFILE is cantor-phase3-topology-receipt/0.3
  + WINDOWS_TOPOLOGY_PROFILE remains cantor-windows-candidate-topology/0.1
  + profile equality remains exact string equality with no prefix, range, alias, or migration

& [TopologyReceiptFieldContract] is exact
  + import InventoryConsistencyEvidence rather than ConsistencyClass
  + remove public field consistency
  + add public required field consistency_evidence of type InventoryConsistencyEvidence in the same semantic position
  + rustdoc states the label is caller-supplied form data until a separately authorized issuer binds its support
  + TopologyReceipt remains caller constructible and serde-capable as a pure form
  + form construction and validation do not become evidence issuance

& [TopologyReceiptAdmissibility] is exact
  + receipt 0.3 permits only InventoryConsistencyEvidence::NonAtomicRepeatedInventoryEqual
  + InventoryConsistencyEvidence::OsSnapshotProven returns TopologyFormFaultCode::Receipt
  + snapshot rejection field is consistency_evidence
  + exact bounded message is receipt 0.3 permits only non_atomic_repeated_inventory_equal
  + no fallback, coercion, downgrade, partial receipt, or alternate grade exists

& [LegacyRejection] is strict
  + otherwise current-shaped receipt with receipt_profile cantor-phase3-topology-receipt/0.2 rejects at receipt_profile
  + JSON field consistency rejects as unknown
  + JSON missing consistency_evidence rejects
  + JSON containing old and new fields rejects
  + JSON value quiescent_double_inventory rejects in any enum position
  + JSON with new field and old token rejects
  + old Rust type and variant names fail compile
  + no decoder rewrite, serde alias, default, migration job, or compatibility shim exists

& [UnchangedTopologyReceiptInvariants] are mandatory
  + scanner_profile remains exact cantor-windows-candidate-topology/0.1
  + candidate_root remains bounded nonempty NUL-free caller text and gains no physical-canonicality proof
  + root_identity remains exact StrongFileIdentity
  + root_volume_guid_path remains exact canonical syntax only
  + admission_profile, admission_receipt_sha256, policy_sha256, scan_nonce, and ordered_inventory_sha256 remain required and bounded
  + TopologyScanLimits remain complete, positive, capped, and relationally valid
  + entry_count remains nonzero and at most maximum_entries
  + total_file_bytes remains at most maximum_total_bytes
  + issued_tick remains less than expires_tick
  + expires_tick remains at or before limits.deadline_tick
  + validation order remains unchanged except for replacing the exact evidence field predicate in place
  + validation remains syntax and relation checking over supplied values

& [ProducerBoundary] is absent and explicit
  + no physical producer record or function is added
  + no acquisition identities, start ticks, completion ticks, or traversal lineages are added
  + WindowsSuppliedOrderedTopologyInventoryDigestReconciliation is not accepted as proof of repeated physical acquisition
  + a future producer must bind two distinct actual acquisition lineages and exact ordered acquisition relation
  + a future producer must prove exact common scanner, policy, root, limits, and encoding scope
  + a future producer may use pure reconciliation only as one subordinate equality check

& [IssuerAndConsumerBoundary] is absent
  + no receipt issuer, signer, output-only receipt, or content-addressing change is added
  + no consumption ledger, freshness clock, uniqueness state, single-use enforcement, work packet, or admission decision is added
  + no candidate is marked safe, clean, stable, quiescent, immutable, eligible, sealed, or promotable

& [FaultContract] is preserved and exact
  + malformed and legacy JSON returns Json through the existing decoder boundary
  + wrong current-shaped receipt profile returns Receipt at receipt_profile
  + OsSnapshotProven returns Receipt at consistency_evidence
  + every fault remains bounded and atomic
  + no fault includes a partial receipt, acquisition carrier, reconciliation, physical observation, or migrated value

& [ImplementationBoundary] is exactly two existing production modules
  + crates/cantor_ecosystem/src/phase3_evidence.rs may change only selected profile, enum, directly related validation target, rustdoc, and tests
  + crates/cantor_ecosystem/src/topology_forms.rs may change only selected profiles, import, receipt field, receipt validation, rustdoc, and tests
  + in-repository current compile callers and fixtures may migrate explicitly as governed support
  + current evidence builders, assertions, manifests, and dependent topology signature references may migrate explicitly
  + crate public glob export behavior remains unchanged
  + no new production module exists
  + Cargo.toml and Cargo.lock remain byte identical

