& [RollbackContract] is exact
  + restore the two production modules, related current tests, and current evidence references to the pre-revision commit
  + restore current evidence authority fields to predecessor canonical paths and signatures if implementation is rolled back
  + remove only implementation and revision closure artifacts
  + retain source, SJS, supersession, and historical proof records
  + no data migration, database cleanup, physical cleanup, receipt invalidation, or external coordination exists

& [StopBoundary] is mandatory
  + stop on source, manifest, phase-lock, or predecessor drift
  + stop if either replacement signature is absent or invalid
  + stop if old type, variant, field, token, or profile remains accepted
  + stop if OsSnapshotProven receipt succeeds
  + stop if supplied equality becomes repeated acquisition proof
  + stop if scanner profile or unrelated receipt behavior changes
  + stop on third production module, alias, migration, default, conversion, extra grade, dependency, unsafe, platform call, filesystem, clock, producer, consumer, effect, stale evidence, or failed proof
  + stop if any physical or effect-bearing test would be required

